license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code and derived results for an audit of three public glaucoma datasets released
  by one laboratory. All 1302 candidate Harvard-GF x Harvard-FairVision pairs were
  compared at the image level; 1031 are the same three-dimensional OCT volume
  distributed under different identifiers. The archive also contains the
  demonstration of what that overlap does to a downstream evaluation, with five
  training runs and paired bootstrap intervals, and the audit of downstream use
  across five bibliographic indexes. No source images and no patient-level data
  are redistributed.
keywords:
  - glaucoma
  - optical coherence tomography
  - data leakage
  - external validation
  - algorithmic fairness
  - reproducibility
